<%# Honest fallback rendered when the interactive RSC client-reference manifests are
    missing at runtime (the documented Rspack limitation, see SPIKE.md). Keeps the demo
    shell intact and replaces the interactive island with a clear, on-brand notice so a
    visitor never sees a blank or broken surface. %>
<%= render "hello_server/styles" %>

<div class="ror-demo-page">
  <%= render "hello_server/hero" %>

  <section class="notice" data-rsc-fallback>
    <p class="badge">Known Rspack limitation</p>
    <h2>The interactive island is not live on this build</h2>
    <p>
      The async server component above renders fine on the server, but its interactive
      client island (the <code>LikeButton</code>) is intentionally not wired up here. The
      current Rspack build does not emit the React Server Components client/server
      manifests that the client-reference path needs at runtime, so rather than ship a
      blank or broken widget we are showing this honest note instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a tracked, documented limitation — not a bug in your setup. The bundler,
      streaming SSR, and server-only RSC compilation are all green; only interactive RSC
      client references are blocked until the Rspack path can provide the required
      manifests. Read the full status in
      <a href="<%= github_source_url("SPIKE.md") %>" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SPIKE.md</a>,
      or follow the upstream work in
      <a href="https://github.com/shakacode/react_on_rails/issues/1828" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">shakacode/react_on_rails#1828</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <%= render "hello_server/cards" %>
</div>
